{
 "_doc": "DEP-06 \"What a yield must say\" (yield-evidence-v9, DEP-18; ruled 2026-11-23). Under yield-evidence-v9 a DisputeYield carries exactly one reason, each 32 bytes: lost_to (TLV 367, a claim txid), reestablished (TLV 369, a QuorumBegin update's content_hash), excluded_by (TLV 371, a confiscation or re-arm spend txid). `wire`: the DisputeYield operation's encoding with each reason (hashes as here: txids in display hex are stored as their wire bytes, i.e. reversed; the reestablished hash as written). `cases`: `fold` is whether a fork under `ruleset` takes the yield (structural: exactly one reason under yield-evidence-v9, anything under an earlier ruleset). `verdict` (valid | invalid | pending) and `why` are the judge's answer, checked in this order: legacy (ruleset without the rule) -> no-reason; lost_to: unconfirmed (unknown or no height), early (its height > yield_height), then the acquire_binding judgment against `vaults` (unconfirmed | not-a-claim | not-this-lottery), earlier-round (the round it closes < arm_round), own-claim (output 0 pays one of the yielder's `targets` or input 1 spends one of its `pledges`); reestablished: not-expiry (the dispute's reason is not quorum_expired), unknown-quorum-begin, not-after-fork-point (seq <= last_valid_sequence), rotation-unconfirmed; excluded_by: unconfirmed, early, the lottery's round walked back like a claim's input (the named tx spends a vault: round 1; a confirmed re-arm-shaped tx spending output 0 of the previous: one more; else not-this-lottery), earlier-round, in-lottery (the yielder's xonly is among `participants`, the set the judge rebuilt for that lottery). txs: `height` null = unconfirmed; `outputs` are scriptPubKeys (hex). arm_round is the yielder's latest arm's round before the yield. Shared by the spec, deposits-rust (deposits-core/tests/vectors/yield_evidence.json) and cl-deposits (inspect/vectors/yield_evidence.json).",
